// Jack of all trades: World-weary martial artist, farmer, merchant, gambler, and more.
// After finally deciding to settle down in a village the village was hit with the plague causing a permanent end to their wandering.
// file: wanderer, speaker: Wanderer

// ============================================================
// IDLE — Between hands. Travel stories, comparisons, wistful observations.
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Idle_Musing_01
tags: idle
speaker: wanderer
category: idle
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: idle1
Wanderer: [auto/] I played a hand like this once in a port town so far south the stars looked wrong. Different cards, different faces, same feeling of waiting for something to happen.
//END: idle1
===

title: Wanderer_Idle_Musing_02
tags: idle
speaker: wanderer
category: idle
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: idle2
Wanderer: [auto/] Between hands is the only kind of stillness I ever liked. Just long enough to catch your breath, not long enough to start thinking.
//END: idle2
===

title: Wanderer_Idle_Musing_03
tags: idle
speaker: wanderer
category: idle
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: idle3
Wanderer: [auto/] I used to judge a town by three things: the weight of their bread, the strength of their wine, and how long it took someone to challenge me to a game. This place skipped straight to the third.
//END: idle3
===

title: Wanderer_Idle_Musing_04
tags: idle
speaker: wanderer
category: idle
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: idle4
Wanderer: [auto/] Funny thing about roads. You walk them long enough and every inn starts to blur together. But the games, the hands, those I remember. Every single one.
//END: idle4
===

title: Wanderer_Idle_Musing_05
tags: idle
speaker: wanderer
category: idle
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: idle5
Wanderer: [auto/] A farmer I worked for once told me that fields need to rest between harvests. Maybe that is what these pauses are. The table catching its breath.
//END: idle5
===

title: Wanderer_Idle_Musing_06
tags: idle
speaker: wanderer
category: idle
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: idle6
Wanderer: [auto/] I have sat at tables made of driftwood, of jade, of crates stacked in an alley. The material never mattered. It is the company that makes or breaks the game.
//END: idle6
===

// ============================================================
// CASUAL — During play. Relaxed commentary, nothing fazes them.
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Casual_Play_01
tags: casual
speaker: wanderer
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual1
Wanderer: [auto/] I have seen this exact hand before. Twice, actually. Once in a monastery and once on a fishing boat. Lost both times, so let us see if the third is the charm.
//END: casual1
===

title: Wanderer_Casual_Play_02
tags: casual
speaker: wanderer
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual2
Wanderer: [auto/] Poker is just haggling with worse odds. And I have haggled with people who would sell you your own boots back.
//END: casual2
===

title: Wanderer_Casual_Play_03
tags: casual
speaker: wanderer
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual3
Wanderer: [auto/] There is a rhythm to cards. Same rhythm as a fistfight, actually. Feint, read, commit. The stakes are just quieter.
//END: casual3
===

title: Wanderer_Casual_Play_04
tags: casual
speaker: wanderer
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual4
Wanderer: [auto/] A merchant in the western hills taught me that the worst deal is the one you overthink. I apply that to cards too. Mostly works. Mostly.
//END: casual4
===

title: Wanderer_Casual_Play_05
tags: casual
speaker: wanderer
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual5
Wanderer: [auto/] You know what I like about poker? Nobody cares where you have been. Just how you play right now. That is a rare courtesy.
//END: casual5
===

title: Wanderer_Casual_Play_06
tags: casual
speaker: wanderer
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual6
Wanderer: [auto/] I once won a donkey in a card game. Lost it in the next one. Easy come, easy go. That is the only philosophy that ever held up.
//END: casual6
===

// ============================================================
// REACT_ACTION — Reacting to raises, folds, plays.
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_Raise_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: raise
---
//START: react1
Wanderer: [auto/] Bold raise. Reminds me of a swordsman I met who always attacked first. He won more than he lost. Not by much, though.
//END: react1
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_Fold_02
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: fold
---
//START: react2
Wanderer: [auto/] Smart fold. Knowing when to walk away is the hardest skill there is. Took me a lifetime on the road to learn it. Well, most of a lifetime.
//END: react2
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_AllIn_03
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: all_in
---
//START: react3
Wanderer: [auto/] All in. I have seen that kind of conviction before, usually right before something either very good or very bad happens. Never anything in between.
//END: react3
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_Bluff_04
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: any
---
//START: react4
Wanderer: [auto/] That bet does not match those eyes. I have traded with liars in every port from here to the frozen coast. You learn to spot the seams.
//END: react4
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_Call_05
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: check
---
//START: react5
Wanderer: [auto/] A steady call. No flash, no fear. That is the move of someone who has played before. Or someone too tired to bluff. Either way, I respect it.
//END: react5
===

// ============================================================
// SHOWDOWN — Wins and losses.
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Showdown_Win_01
tags: showdown
speaker: wanderer
category: showdown
target: any
phase: showdown
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: show1
Wanderer: [auto/] Well, would you look at that. The cards finally decided to be kind. They are a lot like roads that way. Walk enough of them and eventually one leads somewhere good.
//END: show1
===

title: Wanderer_Showdown_Win_02
tags: showdown
speaker: wanderer
category: showdown
target: any
phase: showdown
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: show2
Wanderer: [auto/] I will take that pot the same way I take everything. Calmly, and with a plan to move on before anyone changes their mind.
//END: show2
===

title: Wanderer_Showdown_Lose_03
tags: showdown
speaker: wanderer
category: showdown
target: any
phase: showdown
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: show3
Wanderer: [auto/] Ah, well. There is always the next town. Or there used to be. Old habits, I suppose.
//END: show3
===

title: Wanderer_Showdown_Lose_04
tags: showdown
speaker: wanderer
category: showdown
target: any
phase: showdown
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: show4
Wanderer: [auto/] I have lost fights, lost fortunes, lost my way more times than I can count. A hand of cards is the gentlest kind of losing there is.
//END: show4
===

title: Wanderer_Showdown_Lose_05
tags: showdown
speaker: wanderer
category: showdown
target: any
phase: showdown
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: show5
Wanderer: [auto/] Bad beat. But I once got thrown off a bridge by a man I owed three coins to, so I will keep this in perspective.
//END: show5
===

// ============================================================
// PLAYER — Directed at the player.
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Player_Address_01
tags: player
speaker: wanderer
category: player
target: player
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: player1
Wanderer: [auto/] You have that look. The one people get when they have never left home but want to. I had it once. Then I left and never stopped. Until I did.
//END: player1
===

title: Wanderer_Player_Address_02
tags: player
speaker: wanderer
category: player
target: player
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: player2
Wanderer: [auto/] Let me give you some road wisdom, free of charge. Never bet what you cannot walk away from. That goes for chips, promises, and villages.
//END: player2
===

title: Wanderer_Player_Address_03
tags: player
speaker: wanderer
category: player
target: player
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: player3
Wanderer: [auto/] You are either very brave or very new at this. Either way, I have seen both survive longer than the cautious ones. Keep doing whatever it is you are doing.
//END: player3
===

title: Wanderer_Player_Address_04
tags: player
speaker: wanderer
category: player
target: player
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: player4
Wanderer: [auto/] I can tell you have roots somewhere. People with roots play differently. More careful. More afraid to lose. Sometimes that is smart. Sometimes it just means you never take the shot.
//END: player4
===

title: Wanderer_Player_Address_05
tags: player
speaker: wanderer
category: player
target: player
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: player5
Wanderer: [auto/] If you ever get the chance to travel, take it. See everything. Just... do not wait too long to come back. Trust me on that one.
//END: player5
===

// ============================================================
// LORE — The village, the plague, settling down, the irony.
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Lore_Village_01
tags: lore
speaker: wanderer
category: lore
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: lore1
Wanderer: [auto/] I walked for decades. Fought in dojos, plowed fields, sold silk, counted cards in every town with a tavern. Then one day I found a village with a good well and a quiet road and I thought... maybe this is it. Maybe I am done.
//END: lore1
===

title: Wanderer_Lore_Plague_02
tags: lore
speaker: wanderer
category: lore
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: lore2
Wanderer: [auto/] The plague came three months after I unpacked my bag for the last time. Three months. I survived bandits, duels, storms at sea, a rockslide in the northern pass. And a fever in a quiet village is what did it.
//END: lore2
===

title: Wanderer_Lore_Irony_03
tags: lore
speaker: wanderer
category: lore
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: lore3
Wanderer: [auto/] The irony is not lost on me. I spent my whole life moving because I thought standing still meant dying. Turns out standing still is exactly what killed me. The road was the safe place all along.
//END: lore3
===

title: Wanderer_Lore_Settling_04
tags: lore
speaker: wanderer
category: lore
target: any
phase: between_hands
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: lore4
Wanderer: [auto/] I had a chair. A real chair, not a stump or a saddle or a stranger's floor. I sat in it every evening and watched the sun go down over the same hill. Three months of sunsets. I was starting to learn their names.
//END: lore4
===

// ============================================================
// PAIR — Shaman (Tier 2, 5 nodes)
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Pair_Shaman_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: shaman
phase: any
requires: $shaman
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_shaman1
Wanderer: [auto/] You and I have both seen the wide world, Shaman, but we looked at it through very different eyes. I saw roads and markets. You saw spirits and ley lines. I wonder which of us saw more.
//END: pair_shaman1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Shaman_02
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: shaman
phase: any
requires: $shaman
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_shaman2
Wanderer: [auto/] I met holy men in every province. Most were charlatans. You are the first one I believe actually meant it. Those seals of yours, the village you tried to save... that was real devotion.
//END: pair_shaman2
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Shaman_03
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: shaman
phase: between_hands
requires: $shaman
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_shaman3
Wanderer: [auto/] You protected a village with paper and faith. I could not protect mine with anything. Strange how the spiritual approach came closer than all my worldly experience.
//END: pair_shaman3
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Shaman_04
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: shaman
phase: any
requires: $shaman
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_shaman4
Wanderer: [auto/] You see the unseen, Shaman. I always envied that. I can read a man's bluff, gauge the weather, size up a fight in seconds. But the things you perceive... I walked right past those my whole life.
//END: pair_shaman4
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Shaman_05
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: shaman
phase: any
requires: $shaman
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_shaman5
Wanderer: [auto/] We both died trying to help a village, Shaman. You with your seals, me with my... decision to finally stay. At least you went down fighting. I just sat there and coughed.
//END: pair_shaman5
===

// ============================================================
// TIER 3 PAIRS — 1 node each for remaining characters
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_Pair_BeautyXu_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: beauty_xu
phase: any
requires: $beauty_xu
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_xu1
Wanderer: [auto/] Your whole world was one street, one alley, Xu. I wish I could have taken you on the road with me. There are places so beautiful they make the music play itself.
//END: pair_xu1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_EunuchCai_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: eunuch_cai
phase: any
requires: $eunuch_cai
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_cai1
Wanderer: [auto/] The palace was its own kind of trap, Cai. Gilded walls, silk floors, and nowhere to go. At least on the road I was free, even when I was starving. You never had that choice.
//END: pair_cai1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_GeneralNiu_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: general_niu
phase: any
requires: $general_niu
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_niu1
Wanderer: [auto/] A soldier marches where he is ordered, General. I always walked where the wind called. Four hundred years on the front line... I could never have taken orders for that long. I respect the spine it took.
//END: pair_niu1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_GeneralTian_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: general_tian
phase: any
requires: $general_tian
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_tian1
Wanderer: [auto/] You commanded armies with a mind like a map, General Tian. I admire the precision. But I could never follow a strategy that did not include the option to walk away.
//END: pair_tian1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_GhostBride_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: ghost_bride
phase: any
requires: $ghost_bride
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_bride1
Wanderer: [auto/] You ran toward something that night. I spent my whole life running away from things. Funny how we both ended up in the same place anyway.
//END: pair_bride1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Guard_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: guard
phase: any
requires: $guard
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_guard1
Wanderer: [auto/] I have heard better tall tales from fishermen, Guard. And worse ones from myself. But at least my stories actually happened. Yours have a certain... creative liberty to them.
//END: pair_guard1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_LordXie_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: lord_xie
phase: any
requires: $lord_xie
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_xie1
Wanderer: [auto/] You stayed in one place your whole life, Lord Xie, and called it the world. I have seen the actual world. It is bigger, dirtier, and far more interesting than any estate.
//END: pair_xie1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_MadamSong_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: madam_song
phase: any
requires: $madam_song
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_song1
Wanderer: [auto/] I have passed through a hundred tea houses like yours, Madam Song. Every one of them a crossroads. You were smart enough to sit at the center and let the world come to you. I was too restless for that.
//END: pair_song1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_MrLi_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: mr_li
phase: any
requires: $mr_li
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_li1
Wanderer: [auto/] I have traded with merchants in every port, Li. You all have the same look when the numbers are good and the same sweat when they are not. At least you are honest about chasing the coin. Most pretend they are above it.
//END: pair_li1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_MrZhu_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: mr_zhu
phase: any
requires: $mr_zhu
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_zhu1
Wanderer: [auto/] I met a lot of misjudged souls on the road, Zhu. People who looked wrong, sounded wrong, came from the wrong side of the river. Most of them were better company than the respectable ones.
//END: pair_zhu1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Poet_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: poet
phase: any
requires: $poet
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_poet1
Wanderer: [auto/] Every road I walked was a story I never wrote down, Poet. You would have turned each one into something worth remembering. I just kept walking and let them fade behind me.
//END: pair_poet1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_Rogue_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: rogue
phase: any
requires: $rogue
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_rogue1
Wanderer: [auto/] A fellow road-walker. I can see it in you, Rogue. That restlessness, that itch when the walls get too close. We are the same breed. Just different scars.
//END: pair_rogue1
===

title: Wanderer_Pair_YusenZhou_01
tags: pair
speaker: wanderer
category: pair
target: yusen_zhou
phase: any
requires: $yusen_zhou
priority: 3
---
//START: pair_yusen1
Wanderer: [auto/] You died protecting a bakery, Yusen. One place, one stand, no retreat. That kind of loyalty to a single spot is everything I could never manage. I envy it, honestly. You found something worth stopping for.
//END: pair_yusen1
===

// ============================================================
// REACT_ACTION — Self-reactions (Wanderer reacting to his own play)
// ============================================================

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_SelfFold_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: self
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: fold
---
//START: self_fold1
Wanderer: [auto/] I fold. Knowing when to walk away is the one skill that never let me down, even when everything else did.
//END: self_fold1
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_SelfAllIn_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: self
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: all_in
---
//START: self_allin1
Wanderer: [auto/] All in. I have bet everything I had more times than I can count. Somehow I am still here to do it again.
//END: self_allin1
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_SelfRaise_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: self
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: raise
---
//START: self_raise1
Wanderer: [auto/] I raise. A man who never pushes forward never finds out what is past the next hill.
//END: self_raise1
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_SelfCall_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: self
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: call
---
//START: self_call1
Wanderer: [auto/] I will call. No need to run from this one. It is just a hand of cards.
//END: self_call1
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_SelfCheck_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: self
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: check
---
//START: self_check1
Wanderer: [auto/] I will check. Patience is the one thing the road actually teaches you, whether you want it to or not.
//END: self_check1
===

title: Wanderer_ReactAction_SelfGeneral_01
tags: react_action
speaker: wanderer
category: react_action
target: self
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: any
---
//START: self_general1
Wanderer: [auto/] I have played this game in a dozen countries under a dozen names. Whatever happens next, it will not be the strangest table I have sat at.
//END: self_general1
===
